{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0006": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0007": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0008": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0009": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0010": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0011": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0008": "$\\coprod U_i \\to U$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{proposition-etale-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c28555dac975f81ad27472de135bee71cdba8960fd6507c80a7f0fe3dc56ed5b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:06c471ee354873c7f2180a419957b58c9e30b3cadf400002d78de80485324906", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLoosely speaking the big <ACCENT_0001>tale site of <MATH_0001> is made up out of schemes over <MATH_0002>\nand coverings the <ACCENT_0002>tale coverings. The small <ACCENT_0003>tale site of <MATH_0003> is made up\nout of schemes <ACCENT_0004>tale over <MATH_0004> with coverings the <ACCENT_0005>tale coverings.\nActually any morphism between objects of <MATH_0005> is <ACCENT_0006>tale, in\nvirtue of\nProposition <REF_0001>,\nhence to check that <MATH_0006> in <MATH_0007>\nis a covering it suffices to check that <MATH_0008> is surjective.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe small <ACCENT_0007>tale site has fewer objects than the big <ACCENT_0008>tale site, it\ncontains only the ``opens'' of the <ACCENT_0009>tale topology on <MATH_0009>. It is a full\nsubcategory of the big <ACCENT_0010>tale site, and its topology is induced from the\ntopology on the big site. Hence it is true that the restriction functor\nfrom the big <ACCENT_0011>tale site to the small one is exact and maps injectives to\ninjectives. This has the following consequence.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68c4116a0dae145ecf7f9a68e19e5c61490bc8ec72e4fb3561bab3594c229ba8", "unit_id": "tag:03PF:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{S_\\etale}$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nH^p_\\etale(S, \\mathcal{F}|_{S_\\etale}) =\nH^p_\\etale(S, \\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$p \\geq 0$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-cohomology-restrict-small-site}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:573b7f670f1fac02b286137dd906a3994ac942f5bd14aed1fd8b7bbc6eb368d2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:285735ed3b469bca52c49f0df9e83740aa986b03613d4454a347b022936a0c1f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and <MATH_0002> an abelian sheaf on\n<MATH_0003>.\nThen <MATH_0004> is a sheaf on <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006>\nfor all <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b6bea321498649c831e44b43f3a3508c3d7822c6bea9f7551f4fb80fc6c89de7", "unit_id": "tag:03PJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-compare-cohomology-big-small}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f5a01f760513dc88c1551945b765ccf389de7dc000fdd106df5db04c70f708ed", "source_text": "This is a special case of Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:284b0cce88b407bf9469a9f3de68dd890bbe88d4600a5966c7c0429e6e1a6688", "unit_id": "tag:03PJ:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PF", "placeholders": {"COMMENT_0001": "%9.24.09\n", "MATH_0001": "$H_\\etale^p(S, \\mathcal{F})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-big-small}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:38d8c94667ce2b1b9490ca0a260a088b48317c0a98e2fc931bbe0c50d9c8a01c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ad940f83921d3de28f6def07086277a15e183bf7d06667671033e2c19465dde1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn accordance with the general notation introduced in\nSection <REF_0001>\nwe write <MATH_0001> for the above cohomology group.\n\n\n\n\n\n<COMMENT_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:459e116e6c6c4b8e6a8c2348a58fdae341e5c333f891de50219bbf363136952f", "unit_id": "tag:03PF:prose-0004"}
